# Three QML files copied out of KDE, so the applet depends on nothing a Plasma session does not
# already guarantee.
#
# The popup needs two controls Plasma's own component set does not have: a segmented button and a
# colour button. Both were drawn by hand first, and both looked like what they were. Importing
# them instead meant importing org.kde.kirigamiaddons.components and org.kde.kquickcontrols, which
# was measured as safe by reading the QML import path out of a live plasmashell -- on one machine.
# Which modules a plasmashell carries is a packaging decision each distribution makes for itself,
# and KOSMIC now aims at any of them. A module that turns out to be absent is not a graceful
# degradation: Qt.createComponent returns null, the popup does not open, and the only trace is one
# line in the journal.
#
# Copying is possible because all three are plain QML. Both modules ship a .so beside the .qml,
# but their own qmldir marks it `optional plugin` -- the compiled half is what KeySequenceItem
# needs, not these. The only external import left is org.kde.kirigami, which is the backbone of
# every Plasma UI and is not optional anywhere.
#
#   ColorButton.qml         kdeclarative, org.kde.kquickcontrols          verbatim
#   DefaultContentItem.qml  kirigami-addons, ...kirigamiaddons.delegates  verbatim
#   SegmentedButton.qml     kirigami-addons, ...kirigamiaddons.components one import rewired
#
# SegmentedButton is the only one changed, and in one place: it imported the delegates module for
# DefaultContentItem, which is now the copy beside it. That is also why DefaultContentItem is here
# at all -- it is SegmentedButton's only transitive dependency, and it imports nothing but QtQuick
# and Kirigami.
#
# Copied rather than redrawn for three reasons. The SPDX headers are upstream's and credit their
# authors, so `reuse lint` passes without anything being asserted on their behalf. LGPL and the
# GPL disjunction are both one-way compatible into GPL-3.0-only, which is what KOSMIC ships under.
# And a copy can be diffed against upstream later; something redrawn cannot.
#
# These do not follow upstream. Both are small and have been stable for years, which is what makes
# that acceptable -- re-check them when the applet next misbehaves on a new Plasma.
